{"file":"walkthrough-1.5.0-v2.zip","bytes":120626,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"walkthrough","description":"Render a session or any subject (plugin, marketplace, path) as a self-contained interactive HTML document","version":"1.5.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/ApurvBazari/claude-plugins","keywords":["session-visualization","interactive-html","documentation","diagrams","walkthrough","session-recap","cowork","claude-cowork"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/create/SKILL.md","name":"create","description":"Generate an interactive HTML walkthrough of the current session — a self-contained, explorable document (prose + diagrams + clickable detail) in a fixed house style. Use when the user asks to \"visualize this session\", \"create a walkthrough\", \"walk me through it\", \"walk me through this/that\", \"walk me through what we did\", \"make a session recap/document\", or runs /walkthrough:create. Writes to .claude/walkthrough/ (or a chosen walkthroughs/ folder in a non-git directory).","headings":["Create — Render the Session as an Interactive Document","Step 1: Scope","Step 2: Gather","Step 3: Synthesize the session model","Step 4: Coverage critic","Step 5: Select components","Step 6: Assemble the HTML","Step 6.5: Resolve output base directory","Step 7: Output path (proliferation guard)","Step 8: Gitignore prompt (first run only)","Step 9: Self-check (structure)","Step 10: Write the file","Step 11: Offer to open","Key Rules"],"name_hint":"创建"},{"path":"skills/document/SKILL.md","name":"document","description":"Render any SUBJECT (a plugin, library, subsystem, or the marketplace) as a self-contained interactive HTML document in the walkthrough house style. Use when the user asks to \"document this plugin\", \"make a docs page for <subject>\", \"generate the plugin landing page\", or runs /walkthrough:document <subject>. Reads README + manifest as canonical source. Writes to the path given, default .claude/walkthrough/.","headings":["Document — Render a Subject as an Interactive Document","Step 1: Identify the subject","Step 2: Gather (README + manifest are canonical)","Step 3: Synthesize the subject model","Step 4: Coverage critic","Step 5: Select components","Step 6: Assemble the HTML","Step 7: Output path","Step 8: Self-check (structure)","Step 9: Write the file","Step 10: Offer to open","Key Rules"],"name_hint":"文档"},{"path":"skills/render/SKILL.md","name":"render","description":"Render a structured model already present in this conversation into the house-style HTML, as-is (no session synthesis). Internal building block invoked by other skills/plugins (e.g. lens) that have already assembled a model. Not for users — for a synthesized session recap use /walkthrough:create.","headings":["Render — Assemble a Supplied Model into the House Style","Step 1: Locate the model + output path","Step 2: Run the shared render stages","Key Rules"],"name_hint":"render"},{"path":"skills/update/SKILL.md","name":"update","description":"Refresh an EXISTING walkthrough HTML in place so it reflects new work — reconstructs the prior content from the document, folds in explicitly-named spec/source files, and overwrites the same file as one coherent document. Use when the user asks to \"update the walkthrough\", \"refresh the session doc\", \"regenerate the walkthrough with the new spec\", or runs /walkthrough:update. Reads from and writes to .claude/walkthrough/.","headings":["Update — Refresh an Existing Walkthrough In Place","Step 1: Resolve the target (always confirm — the overwrite safety gate)","Step 2: Reconstruct the prior model","Step 3: Gather the new material (named files only)","Step 4: Merge into one coherent model","Step 5: Coverage critic","Step 6: Select components","Step 7: Assemble the HTML","Step 8: Self-check (structure)","Step 9: Write in place","Step 10: Offer to open","Key Rules"],"name_hint":"更新"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["walkthrough","Ins